{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3336","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3336","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3336\",\"parent_revision\":\"c06fad17d1e4d37b127a6b5f420b4f68d0fcf1bc\",\"root_revision\":\"5d6450b0fd59001dadc9cc76f54ede5e88190b4ba408bdb82972ac8b49189641\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe root cause behind #3329's deletion, generalized: `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` re-explained MCP tool parameters and return shapes in hand-written prose that the tool's own docstring/`Field(description=...)` annotations already stated \u2014 and that duplicate was structurally guaranteed to drift, because FastMCP regenerates the live tool schema from the code every server start, while a prose copy in a skill file changes only when someone remembers to edit it. That mechanism is what produced the deleted skill's \\\"12 tools\\\" heading against 28 real ones, a dead storage-format claim, and a broken `fastmcp` invocation example.\\n\\nConfirmed during #3329 this isn't unique to that one skill: `plugins/development-harness/README.md`'s \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table has the identical shape (filed separately as #3335).\\n\\nGoal: audit other `dh:*` skills for the same pattern \u2014 prose that restates an MCP tool's parameters, return fields, or behavior, checkable live against the tool's actual schema via `ToolSearch`. Where found: delete the restatement from the skill, and if a genuine content gap exists, add it to the tool's own docstring instead (verified in #3329 to be the correct destination \u2014 it's literally the schema the agent is shown when deciding how to call the tool, a stronger and self-maintaining hook that a skill-file restatement can never be).\\n\\nUser-provided context: see #3329 for the full investigation this generalizes from, including three concrete examples where this exact check (comparing a doc's claim against the live `ToolSearch` schema) revealed the doc was either already redundant or actively wrong.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:43:13.508056Z</sub>\\n\\n## Claim 1: artifact_register enum coverage in create-artifact/SKILL.md\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (documentation incomplete and contradictory instruction)\\n\\nclaim: Skill file lists only 7 of 10 live `artifact_type` enum values, missing `dispatch-plan` and `audit-report`. Skill also explicitly instructs agents never to pass `artifact_type=\\\"task-plan\\\"` even though `task-plan` is a valid enum member on the live schema.\\n\\nevidence:\\n- Live `artifact_register` schema enum contains 10 values: feature-context, architect, task-plan, T0-baseline, TN-verification, codebase-analysis, code-review, research, dispatch-plan, audit-report\\n- Skill file table (lines 61-68) documents only 7 types: feature-context, codebase-analysis, code-review, architect, T0-baseline, TN-verification, research (omits dispatch-plan, audit-report, and task-plan from table)\\n- Skill file section \\\"task-plan\\\" (lines 128-132) redirects users away from `artifact_register`: \\\"Task plans live exclusively in SAM plan storage. Create them with `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan(...)` and retrieve them with `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan(...)`\\\" \u2014 contradicting the valid schema enum value\\n\\nsource:\\n- Live: `artifact_register` enum parameter (ToolSearch)\\n- Skill: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/create-artifact/SKILL.md lines 128-132\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Claim 2: backlog_update milestone parameter in groom-milestone/SKILL.md\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (documentation claims unsupported feature)\\n\\nclaim: Skill file (line 89) states `backlog_update(selector, ...)` can \\\"assign milestone,\\\" but live `backlog_update` schema has no `milestone` parameter.\\n\\nevidence:\\n- Skill file line 89 lists tool as: \\\"`backlog_update(selector, ...)` \u2014 assign milestone, update item fields\\\"\\n- Live `backlog_update` schema parameters: content, description, entry_id, plan, reason, replace_section, section, selector, status, title, verified \u2014 no `milestone` parameter present\\n- Schema is silent on milestone assignment through backlog_update\\n\\nsource:\\n- Live: `backlog_update` parameters (ToolSearch)\\n- Skill: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md line 89\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Claim 3: #-prefixed beads nanoid selector format in implement-feature/SKILL.md\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED (claim supported through schema pattern inference)\\n\\nclaim: Comment (lines 142-143) states \\\"#\\\"-prefixed beads nanoids fail to resolve as a `selector` parameter: \\\"No '#' prefix: find_item resolves a bare GitHub number or a bare beads nanoid, but a '#'-prefixed nanoid resolves neither.\\\"\\n\\nevidence:\\n- Skill file comment (lines 142-143): \\\"No '#' prefix: find_item resolves a bare GitHub number or a bare beads nanoid, but a '#'-prefixed nanoid resolves neither.\\\"\\n- Live `backlog_groom` selector parameter description lists valid formats: \\\"GitHub issue URL, #N, bare number, or title substring, or beads nanoid (e.g. bd-a3f8)\\\"\\n- Schema separates formats: `#N` (for numbers only) and `beads nanoid (e.g. bd-a3f8)` (shown without # prefix)\\n- The schema example `bd-a3f8` (not `#bd-a3f8`) supports the skill's claim that # does not pair with beads nanoids\\n\\nsource:\\n- Live: `backlog_groom` selector parameter description (ToolSearch)\\n- Skill: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md lines 142-143\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:47:54.073340Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: GAP\\nclaim: `backlog_groom` returns `mark_groomed_skipped`/`mark_groomed_skip_reason` fields\\nevidence: Tool schema docstring at server.py:2615-2617 states \\\"Returns: Dict with groomed item title, synced status, and output messages/warnings.\\\" However, the actual implementation at operations.py:3776-3777 shows these fields ARE returned by groom_item() when mark_groomed=True and the re-parsed item lookup fails. Lines shown: `result[\\\"mark_groomed_skipped\\\"] = True` and `result[\\\"mark_groomed_skip_reason\\\"] = f\\\"Item '{selector}' not found in re-parsed backlog\\\"`.\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:3771-3789 (groom_item function), plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2615-2617 (tool schema docstring)\\n\\n---\\n\\nverdict: STALE\\nclaim: `backlog_resolve` response contains a `milestone` field\\nevidence: Tool schema docstring at server.py:2416-2418 states \\\"Returns: Dict with resolved item title, summary, and output messages/warnings.\\\" The actual implementation at operations.py:3386 returns `{\\\"title\\\": item.title, \\\"resolved\\\": True, \\\"summary\\\": summary, **out.to_dict()}`. No `milestone` field is present or constructed in the resolve_item() function. This claim is fabricated and does not appear in the actual response payload.\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:3306-3386 (resolve_item function), plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2416-2418 (tool schema docstring)\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T09:48:18.754462Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: chore: Audit other dh:* skills for hand-written MCP tool documentation that duplicates and drifts from live tool schemas\\nDate: 2026-08-30\\nGoal: Find and fix (or file) other dh:* skills that restate MCP tool parameters/return shapes in prose that drifts from the live ToolSearch schema, the same mechanism that caused #3329's \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current inventory of dh:* skill directories under plugins/development-harness/skills/ (post-#3329 deletion count) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Which of those skills (SKILL.md + bundled references/agents files) contain prose naming or describing an MCP tool's parameters, return fields, or behavior | Status: DERIVABLE\\n3. For each candidate hit, whether the live tool schema (via ToolSearch) already states the same thing verbatim/equivalently (REDUNDANT), contradicts it (STALE), or omits it (GAP) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. Whether any confirmed GAP is small enough to relocate into the tool's own docstring inline during this task, versus large enough to warrant its own follow-up item | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Whether #3335 (README table) or #3329 (deleted dh:backlog skill) overlap with any candidate found here (they should be excluded, already tracked/closed) | Status: AVAILABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:54:54.636717Z</sub>\\n\\n## RT-ICA Assessment: Wave 2 Completeness Review\\n\\n**Assessment Date:** 2026-08-30\\n**Assessor Role:** dh:rtica-assessor (Wave 2 evaluation)\\n\\n### Verdict: **READY**\\n\\n### Condition Status Summary\\n\\nAll five conditions from the RT-ICA Snapshot are satisfied at sufficient maturity for planning:\\n\\n1. **Current inventory of dh:* skill directories (post-#3329 deletion count)** \u2014 AVAILABLE\\n   - Impact Radius Wave 1 confirms the baseline state via independent file review\\n   - 42 files reviewed across 15+ skills + workflow references\\n\\n2. **Which skills contain prose naming/describing MCP tool parameters/return fields/behavior** \u2014 DERIVABLE\\n   - Fact-Check Wave 1 + Wave 2 (two passes by independent fact-checkers) identified exact locations\\n   - Three VERIFIED claims with file/line citations (artifact_register, backlog_update, selector format)\\n   - Two additional candidate gaps flagged in Impact Radius (mark_groomed_skipped duplication, backlog_resolve milestone claim)\\n\\n3. **For each candidate: whether live tool schema contradicts it (REDUNDANT/STALE/GAP)** \u2014 DERIVABLE\\n   - Claim 1.0.0 (artifact_register): VERIFIED \u2014 3 missing enum values + contradictory task-plan guidance\\n   - Claim 1.0.1 (backlog_update milestone): VERIFIED \u2014 parameter does not exist on live schema\\n   - Claim 1.0.2 (selector format): VERIFIED \u2014 claim correct, schema inference confirms\\n   - Claim 1.1a (backlog_groom mark_groomed fields): GAP \u2014 fields exist in code, not documented\\n   - Claim 1.1b (backlog_resolve milestone): STALE \u2014 field does not exist (fabricated claim)\\n\\n4. **Whether confirmed GAPs are small enough to relocate into tool docstring vs. warrant follow-up item** \u2014 DERIVABLE\\n   - Artifact_register enum gaps (3 values) \u2014 sufficiently bounded for inline docstring addition\\n   - Backlog_update milestone parameter \u2014 no real capability, only doc error to remove\\n   - Backlog_groom mark_groomed fields \u2014 single return field with clear semantics, docstring-relocatable\\n   - Backlog_resolve milestone claim \u2014 confirmed fabrication, simple removal task\\n\\n5. **Overlap check: whether #3335/#3329 or already-closed findings surface in this item's scope** \u2014 AVAILABLE\\n   - Wave 1 Impact Radius confirms no overlap with #3335 (README table, separate) or #3329 (deleted skill, absent)\\n   - Two scope-expansion candidates identified as distinct from Wave 0's four named files\\n   - No rework of previously closed patterns detected\\n\\n### Fact-Check Verdict Distribution\\n\\n- **VERIFIED (3 claims):** Claims correctly state behavior that live schema either omits or contradicts\\n- **GAP (1 claim):** Behavior exists in code but live docstring is incomplete\\n- **STALE (1 claim):** Claim fabricated; field does not exist in actual implementation\\n\\nThe STALE verdict was anticipated and correctly identified within the Impact Radius scope-expansion section. No REFUTED claims mark any condition MISSING.\\n\\n### Scope-Expansion Assessment\\n\\nWave 1 Impact Radius identified two new candidate gaps requiring fact-checker validation before grooming can assign them to tasks:\\n\\n1. **mark_groomed_skipped field duplication** (finalize.md + groomer-output-validation.md) \u2014 same claim in two files, coordination risk if behavior changes\\n2. **backlog_resolve milestone field** (close/start.md) \u2014 needs source verification before deciding if field actually exists\\n\\nBoth are contained and ready for delegation to Wave 2's planning phase.\\n\\n### Readiness Conclusion\\n\\n**Item Status: READY FOR PLANNING**\\n\\n- All five RT-ICA conditions are satisfied (AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE)\\n- Fact-Check provided expected drift patterns with clear evidence\\n- Impact Radius established scope boundary (42 files, 2 scope-expansion items)\\n- No missing information blocks progress to task decomposition\\n- Scope is proportionate to P1 priority (audit + documentation corrections + docstring relocation)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:44:22.608350Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: recurring-pattern\\n\\n**Rationale**: The same mechanism (hand-written MCP tool parameters/return shapes in skill prose drifting from live ToolSearch schemas) has appeared 2+ times: #3329 (deleted dh:backlog skill with \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect), #3335 (README.md Core backlog tools table), plus 3+ confirmed new instances in Wave 0 research (create-artifact/SKILL.md, groom-milestone/SKILL.md, implement-feature/SKILL.md). This is structural drift, not a one-off bug.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: RCA via backlog history keyword search (MCP tool documentation drift patterns, hand-written schema restatement, skill doc staleness) across resolved items to measure frequency. Secondary signal: cross-reference #1113 (agent name reference audit), #1161 (section access pattern incompleteness), #1672 (doc-drift-auditor scope gap) \u2014 all reflect the same root cause: documentation maintaining its own copy of source-of-truth data instead of referencing it.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Skills and README files that restate MCP tool parameters \u2192 instead, delete prose duplicates and relocate genuine content gaps into tool docstrings (single source of truth, regenerated every server start, visible to agents via ToolSearch).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:44:51.057494Z</sub>\\n\\n**Wave 1 impact analysis \u2014 affected-systems inventory**\\n\\nMethod: independently re-verified Wave 0's three confirmed findings against live `ToolSearch` schemas (`backlog_update`, `backlog_list_issues`, `artifact_register`), then extended the sweep into the files Wave 0 flagged as \\\"not exhaustively covered\\\" \u2014 `dispatch/SKILL.md`, `interop/SKILL.md`, `multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` + `references/dispatch-flow.md`, and the full `work-backlog-item/references/workflows/` tree (25 files) + `work-backlog-item/maintenance/github-integration-validation.md` \u2014 plus 15 additional top-level skill files that grepped positive for MCP tool names (`add-new-feature`, `code-review-architecture`, `complete-milestone`, `context-integration`, `discovery`, `execution`, `final-verification`, `forensic-review`, `groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md`, `groom-milestone/references/dispatch-plan-schema.md`, `group-items-to-milestone`, `implementation-manager`, `planning`, `start-task`, `subagent-contract`, `task-decomposition`, `work-milestone` + `references/worktree-worker-protocol.md`). 42 files total reviewed with tool-name context.\\n\\n**RE-VERIFIED (independent confirmation of Wave 0 findings)**\\n\\n- `create-artifact/SKILL.md` \u2014 read lines 50-139 directly. Confirms Wave 0 exactly: the `artifact_type` table (lines 56-68) lists 7 values; live `artifact_register` schema enum has 10 (`feature-context, architect, task-plan, T0-baseline, TN-verification, codebase-analysis, code-review, research, dispatch-plan, audit-report`) \u2014 table omits `task-plan`, `dispatch-plan`, `audit-report`. Lines 128-132 state \\\"Task plans live exclusively in SAM plan storage\\\" and instruct agents to use `sam_plan` instead of `artifact_register` for `task-plan` \u2014 directly contradicting the live enum, which lists `task-plan` as valid. Confirmed CONTRADICTION, not just omission.\\n- `groom-milestone/SKILL.md` lines 86-89 \u2014 confirmed against live `backlog_update` schema (fields: `content, description, entry_id, plan, reason, replace_section, section, selector, status, title, verified` \u2014 no `milestone` field). The line \\\"`backlog_update(selector, ...)` \u2014 assign milestone, update item fields\\\" is unsupported by any current parameter. Also confirmed `backlog_list_issues`'s `milestone` param is `string` type (\\\"Filter by milestone title\\\"), not the numeric `N` the skill's example implies.\\n\\n**SCOPE_EXPANSION: two new candidate gaps found outside Wave 0's four files \u2014 not confirmed drift, need fact-check before remediation.**\\n\\n1. **`work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` line 289 AND `groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md` lines 94-101 (duplicated across two files)** \u2014 both restate that `backlog_groom`'s response carries a `mark_groomed_skipped` (and `mark_groomed_skip_reason`) field signaling the post-write status-advance silently failed. The live `backlog_groom` docstring only promises \\\"groomed item title, synced status, and output messages/warnings\\\" \u2014 it does not document this field. This is the same \\\"GAP\\\" pattern as Wave 0's `implement-feature` finding (real behavior the schema is silent on) but it is asserted identically in *two* separate skill files, meaning it must be kept in sync in two places if the field's behavior ever changes \u2014 a duplication risk on top of the gap. Needs a fact-checker to confirm the field's actual existence/behavior against source before deciding whether to relocate it into the tool docstring (per this item's stated remediation direction) or leave both restatements as-is.\\n2. **`work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md` line 220** \u2014 \\\"Read the `milestone` field from the `backlog_resolve` response.\\\" Live `backlog_resolve` docstring only documents \\\"resolved item title, summary, and output messages/warnings\\\" \u2014 no `milestone` field is named. Unlike the `groom-milestone`/`backlog_update` finding, this can't be confirmed as *contradicted* (the docstring is a loose prose summary, not an exhaustive return schema), so it's CANDIDATE GAP, not CONFIRMED \u2014 needs a live `backlog_resolve` call or source read to verify the field actually exists before treating it as ground truth.\\n\\n**CHECKED, NOT AN ISSUE (bare invocation only, no parameter/behavior restatement at risk)**\\n\\n`dispatch/SKILL.md`, `interop/SKILL.md`, `multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` + `references/dispatch-flow.md`, `add-new-feature/SKILL.md`, `task-decomposition/SKILL.md`, `execution/SKILL.md`, `start-task/SKILL.md`, `implementation-manager/SKILL.md`, `context-integration/SKILL.md`, `complete-milestone/SKILL.md`, `code-review-architecture/SKILL.md`, `group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md`, `groom-milestone/references/dispatch-plan-schema.md`, and all 25 files of the `work-backlog-item/references/workflows/` tree except the one gap noted above \u2014 every tool-name hit in these files is a bare invocation example (selector/section/content passed through) or an accurate one-line paraphrase, not a restated parameter table, enum, or return-shape claim that live schema could contradict. This matches Wave 0's characterization; the broader sweep did not surface additional same-pattern (#3329-shape) drift beyond the three files Wave 0 already named.\\n\\n**Not reached this wave**: `code-review-architecture/SKILL.md`, `code-review-claude-skills`, `code-review-cli/llm/nodejs/python/typescript/web`, `codebase-auditor`, `codemod-runner`, `ecosystem-research`, `evaluate-sdlc-layers`, `fact-check`, `file-classification`, `find-cause`, `gate-push`, `generate-task`, `kage-bunshin`, `meta-workflow-graph-refresh`, `planner-rt-ica`, `research-note`, `review-verdict-contract`, `rt-ica`, `setup-skill-discovery`, `test-failure-mindset`, `validation-protocol`, `verify-done` \u2014 grepped by Wave 0's original tool-name pattern with zero hits in the initial directory scan, so not independently re-verified in this wave. Low risk (no tool-name mentions means no restatement possible) but flagging for completeness.\\n\\n**Overlap check**: no new file overlaps with #3335 (README table) or #3329 (deleted skill, absent from tree). The two new candidate-gap files (`close/start.md`, `groomer-output-validation.md`/`finalize.md`) are distinct from all four of Wave 0's named files.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:38:33.138074Z</sub>\\n\\n**Wave 0 pre-swarm research \u2014 hand-written MCP tool documentation drift in dh:* skills**\\n\\nMethod: enumerated all `plugins/development-harness/skills/*/` directories (63 post-#3329), grepped SKILL.md + `references/*.md` + `agents/*.md` across all of them for MCP tool names (`backlog_view`, `backlog_groom`, `backlog_list_issues`, `backlog_update`, `artifact_register`, `artifact_read`, `artifact_list`, `sam_task`, `sam_plan`, etc.), filtered bare-invocation mentions (not a drift risk) from prose that names/describes parameters, return fields, or behavior, then compared each candidate hit against the live schema via `ToolSearch(\\\"select:<tool>\\\")` and one live `backlog_view` call.\\n\\n**CONFIRMED \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/create-artifact/SKILL.md` (STALE + GAP, high confidence)**\\n\\nThis entire skill file exists to restate `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_register`'s parameters and return shape in prose. It has already drifted the same way the deleted `dh:backlog` skill did (#3329):\\n\\n- Lines 56-68, \\\"## Parameters > `artifact_type`\\\" table lists 7 recognized type strings: `feature-context`, `codebase-analysis`, `code-review`, `architect`, `T0-baseline`, `TN-verification`, `research`. The live `artifact_register` schema's `artifact_type` field is an enum of **10** values \u2014 the table omits `task-plan`, `dispatch-plan`, and `audit-report` entirely. `dispatch-plan` and `audit-report` are not mentioned anywhere else in the file either \u2014 silent drift, structurally identical to #3329's \\\"12 tools vs 28\\\" defect.\\n- Lines 128-132 go further and are actively **contradictory**: \\\"Task plans live exclusively in SAM plan storage\u2026 Create them with `sam_plan`\\\" \u2014 instructing agents never to pass `artifact_type=\\\"task-plan\\\"` to `artifact_register` \u2014 while the live schema lists `task-plan` as a valid `artifact_type` enum member for that exact tool. Either the tool's enum is stale (still exposes a value the skill says is invalid) or the skill's guidance is stale (the tool now supports it); either way this is a direct, checkable contradiction between skill prose and live schema, not just an omission.\\n- Lines 24-52 (\\\"## Invocation\\\" and the return-value paragraph) restate `item_id`, `artifact_type`, `artifact_id`, `status` (enum `draft|current|superseded|archived`, default `\\\"current\\\"`), `agent` (default `\\\"\\\"`), `content` (required, non-empty), and the return dict shape (`registered`, `artifact_count`, `action` \u2208 {\\\"added\\\",\\\"updated\\\"}, `content_stored`, `messages`, `warnings`). Checked against the live docstring/schema \u2014 this part is REDUNDANT (accurate, near-verbatim duplicate) rather than stale, but it's the same duplication mechanism that produced the `artifact_type` table drift above: hand-copied schema that only updates when someone remembers to.\\n\\nRecommendation: this file is the strongest candidate for the remediation this item calls for \u2014 delete the `artifact_type` table and the Invocation parameter restatement (redundant with live schema), fix or resolve the `task-plan` contradiction (verify current tool behavior first), and keep only what `ToolSearch` cannot provide: the CLI-equivalent invocation, the \\\"when to use this skill vs sam_plan\\\" trigger guidance, and the producing-agent-per-type mapping (arguably a genuine content addition \u2014 recommend relocating into the `artifact_type` enum member descriptions in the tool schema itself rather than the skill, per this item's stated destination-of-record).\\n\\n**CONFIRMED \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` lines 86-89 (STALE, medium confidence)**\\n\\n\\\"## MCP Tools Used\\\" one-line list:\\n```\\n- `backlog_list_issues(milestone=N)` \u2014 load milestone items and groomed status\\n- `backlog_view(selector)` \u2014 read individual item Impact Radius and metadata\\n- `backlog_groom(selector)` \u2014 trigger grooming for ungroomed items\\n- `backlog_update(selector, ...)` \u2014 assign milestone, update item fields\\n```\\n`backlog_update`'s live schema has no `milestone` parameter at all \u2014 its fields are `content`, `description`, `entry_id`, `plan`, `reason`, `replace_section`, `section`, `selector`, `status`, `title`, `verified`. The claim \\\"assign milestone\\\" is not supported by any parameter on this tool as currently schema'd \u2014 either milestone assignment happens through a different, unnamed mechanism, or this line is stale. Needs a fact-checker follow-up to confirm which.\\n\\nLower-confidence secondary note on the same block: `backlog_list_issues(milestone=N)` \u2014 the live `milestone` param is typed `string`, described \\\"Filter by milestone title\\\", not a numeric ID; the skill's `N` naming may mislead an agent into passing an integer. `backlog_groom(selector) \u2014 \\\"trigger grooming\\\"` is a loose paraphrase (the live tool is a content-write/sync operation, not an action-trigger) but low-stakes as a one-line tools-used pointer.\\n\\n**CANDIDATE GAP \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 148-155 (unverified, needs fact-check)**\\n\\nInline comment on a `backlog_groom` call: `{issue}` is `str | int`... \\\"No '#' prefix: find_item resolves a bare GitHub number or a bare beads nanoid, but a '#'-prefixed nanoid resolves neither.\\\" The live `backlog_groom`/`backlog_update`/`backlog_view` `selector` field description (\\\"GitHub issue URL, #N, bare number, or title substring, or beads nanoid\\\") does not capture this specific nanoid-prefix failure mode. This reads as a genuine operational GAP (real caller-facing behavior the schema omits) rather than redundant restatement \u2014 but it was not independently verified against `find_item`'s source in this pass; recommend Wave 1 fact-checker confirm the claim before treating it as ground truth to relocate into the tool docstring.\\n\\n**CHECKED, NOT AN ISSUE \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/dh-meta-docs/references/artifact-conventions.md` lines 78-81**\\n\\n\\\"`backlog_view(selector, summary=false)` \u2014 returns full item context including `sections` dict (groomed fields), labels, and priority.\\\" Verified against a live `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#3336\\\", summary=False)` call in this session \u2014 the response does include `sections`, `labels`, and `priority` top-level keys. REDUNDANT (accurate today) \u2014 carries the same future-drift risk as any hand-copied schema summary, but not currently wrong. Not a remediation priority.\\n\\n**Overlap check**: neither #3335 (README.md \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table) nor #3329 (deleted `dh:backlog` skill, no longer present in this tree) intersect with any file listed above \u2014 confirmed by directory listing, `dh:backlog` skill directory does not exist post-#3329, and `create-artifact`/`groom-milestone`/`implement-feature`/`dh-meta-docs` are all distinct skills from the README and the deleted skill.\\n\\n**Not exhaustively covered**: `dispatch`, `interop`, `multi-perspective-review`, and the `work-backlog-item` workflow reference tree (60+ files) were grepped for tool-name mentions but most hits there are bare invocation examples (selector/section/content passed through), not parameter/behavior restatement, and were not individually diffed against live schemas at `standard` depth \u2014 a `deep`-depth follow-up pass could extend coverage there if the groomer/RT-ICA assessor judges the three confirmed findings above insufficient to close the item.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:54:02.031088Z</sub>\\n\\nMISSION_ALIGNED\\n\\n**Verdict:** This item perfectly aligns with development-harness design principles and continues established precedent from #3329.\\n\\n**Mission Alignment:**\\nThe development-harness is built on the principle that \\\"the harness owns the *process*; language plugins own the *specialists*\\\" (AGENTS.md, line 17). A critical corollary from the artifact system design (AGENTS.md, lines 134\u2013195) is that tooling authority should be singular and self-maintaining: MCP tool docstrings (delivered via FastMCP schemas shown to agents at decision-making time) are the authoritative runtime reference, not hand-written prose copies in skill files.\\n\\n**Design Principle Enforcement:**\\nThis item enforces AGENTS.md's core rule on artifact management: \\\"Every stage produces a logical handoff. Document artifacts use `artifact_register` and `artifact_read`; plans and task state use `sam_plan` and `sam_task`. Neither surface exposes direct filesystem paths\\\" (line 18). Extending this: neither should skill prose duplicate tool schemas. The tool's docstring IS the interface agents see when calling ToolSearch \u2014 it is the strongest possible hook, regenerated fresh each server start from live source code via FastMCP.\\n\\n**Precedent and Pattern:**\\nPR #3329 (merged) established this exact remediation pattern: identify hand-written MCP schema prose in skills, delete the restatement, relocate genuine content gaps into tool docstrings (`backlog_core/server.py` docstrings). That PR identified `dh:backlog` skill's SKILL.md as a drift-prone mirror (12 tools documented vs. 28 real ones, contradictions, dead format claims). The item description correctly cites #3329 as precedent and generalizes its method to other dh:* skills.\\n\\n**Scope Validation:**\\nThe Impact Radius identifies 42 files swept and confirms Wave 0's three drift findings:\\n- `create-artifact/SKILL.md`: enum table lists 7 artifact types; live schema has 10 \u2014 contradictory, not just stale\\n- `groom-milestone/SKILL.md`: documents a `milestone` field on `backlog_update` that doesn't exist in live schema\\n- `implement-feature/SKILL.md`: (Wave 0 finding, included for pattern completeness)\\n\\nTwo candidate gaps flagged for fact-check before remediation are correctly scoped as CANDIDATE, not confirmed drift \u2014 appropriate due diligence. No files overlap with #3335 (README table) or #3329 (deleted skill).\\n\\n**System Strengthening:**\\nDeleting redundant prose from skills and relocating genuine documentation gaps to tool docstrings directly improves the system's maintainability. Tool docstrings are regenerated from live `Field(description=...)` annotations on every server start \u2014 they cannot drift by definition. Skill prose can only drift. This is a zero-loss, pure-gain consolidation toward the single source of truth that the SAM/ARL architecture requires.\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from #3329 (dh:backlog dead-skill cleanup)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:46:16.734461Z</sub>\\n\\n**Frequency Measurement**\\n\\nResolved backlog items with keyword matches (doc drift, skill staleness, schema mismatch): 4 identified across repo history:\\n- #3329 (resolved): deleted dh:backlog skill due to hand-written tool count (\\\"12 tools\\\") drifting from live FastMCP schema (28 tools)\\n- #1113 (groomed): agent name reference drift \u2014 discovered when skill files + Python functions referenced agent names not present in plugin manifest\\n- #1161 (groomed): BacklogItem.sections field added to live code but consumers (agent skill files) never updated \u2014 schema-consumer mismatch\\n- #1672 (groomed): doc-drift-auditor audit gap \u2014 modified files checked but reference docs not checked; allows stale references to remain in doc constellation\\n\\nConfidence: HIGH. #3329 and #3335 are direct instances of **this exact problem**; #1113, #1161, #1672 are the **enabling structural issues** (no validation layer prevents consumer-producer drift).\\n\\n**Root Cause**\\n\\nSkill files, README tables, and agent instructions manually restate MCP tool parameters, return fields, and behavior in prose. This practice violates a core principle: schemas should have a single source of truth, regenerated from code, never hand-copied. Hand-written copies are structurally guaranteed to drift because:\\n\\n1. **FastMCP regenerates live schemas on every server start** \u2014 the tool's `artifact_register`, `backlog_view`, etc. docstrings and field descriptions are derived directly from Python `Field(description=...)` annotations and pydantic models.\\n2. **Skill files are manually maintained** \u2014 a prose copy in `plugins/development-harness/skills/create-artifact/SKILL.md` lines 56-68 is hand-edited and only changes when someone remembers to update it.\\n3. **No enforcement mechanism exists** \u2014 no pre-commit hook, no skilllint rule, no validation gate checks whether prose claims match live schema.\\n4. **Drift is invisible** \u2014 until an agent or user is harmed (wrong parameter list, contradictory guidance, missing enum member), the staleness persists silently.\\n\\n**Enabling structural issues**:\\n- No single-source-of-truth enforcement for tool documentation (agent skill files restate docstrings instead of referencing them)\\n- ToolSearch schema is authoritative and regenerated, but skill files have no annotation to declare \\\"this section is stale, consult ToolSearch instead\\\"\\n- No validation layer (pre-commit hook, skilllint rule, MCP schema audit) catches producer-consumer divergence\\n- Agents are not instructed to use ToolSearch for tool reference instead of searching prose skill files\\n\\n**Improvement**\\n\\nSystemic fix (prevents recurrence):\\n1. **Delete hand-written MCP tool parameter tables from all skill files** \u2014 move this data into tool docstrings (the source of truth, visible to agents via ToolSearch)\\n2. **Update skill files to reference, not restate** \u2014 \\\"See ToolSearch select:artifact_register for current parameters\\\" instead of pasting the table\\n3. **Add skilllint rule** (or pre-commit hook) to detect when skill files mention MCP tool names \u2014 flag as WARN unless the mention is bare (e.g., call example) and not a restatement of parameters/return fields\\n4. **Document destination of record**: tool docstrings (pydantic `Field(description=...)`, function docstrings) are where schema gaps and genuine operational details belong, not skill files\\n\\nImmediate tasks (from Wave 0 findings):\\n- `create-artifact/SKILL.md`: delete `artifact_type` table (stale, 7\u219210 enum values), delete Invocation parameters (redundant), fix or resolve task-plan contradiction via tool inspection\\n- `groom-milestone/SKILL.md`: fact-check backlog_update milestone parameter claim, correct MCP Tools Used list\\n- `implement-feature/SKILL.md`: fact-check nanoid prefix behavior claim against find_item source before promoting to tool docstring\\n\\n**Prevention metric**: Once fixed, run the Wave 0 audit method monthly: enumerate all `dh:*` skills, grep for MCP tool names with parameter/behavior descriptions, spot-check 3-5 hits against live ToolSearch. When zero hits are STALE or REDUNDANT for 2 consecutive months, declare pattern resolved.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"67b46bebcbe260a05cdc666250956490eb9e4f6d19872fc61e9a5a3b1ee3f592\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRe7pGw\"}"}